//~ FLICK-T040 @8:16-8:41 this `if` returns the opposite of its condition
//~ FLICK-T041 @11:21-11:29 an `if not` with an `else`: the condition without `not` reads directly
//~ FLICK-T042 @17:5-17:31 an `if` alone in an `else`: `else if` says it without nesting
//~ FLICK-T043 @20:14-20:20 the literal is on the left of `==`: the value compared reads first
//~ FLICK-T043 @23:17-23:23 the literal is on the left of `>`: the value compared reads first
//~ FLICK-T044 @26:16-26:22 `x` compared with itself is always `true`
//~ FLICK-T045 @29:16-29:20 this condition is always `true`
//~ FLICK-T046 @32:14-34:15 a `match` on a `Bool`: `if` says it directly
